WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.528 --> 00:00:03.028
(tense music)

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.330
- [Narrator] From major
retailers to luxury stores

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:14.280
and small businesses,
organized retail crime,

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:18.270
also known as ORC, has been
on the rise for several years,

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:21.520
with a spike in incidents
over the last few weeks.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.510
ORC incidents involve
any form of retail theft

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:28.153
by an organized group, from
shoplifting to cargo theft.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:32.300
Recently, there has been
a spike in smash and grab

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.030
organized retail crime where large groups

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:36.890
smash display windows and can steal

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:40.640
thousands of dollars in
merchandise within minutes.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.710
- I probably saw 50 to 80
people and like ski mask,

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.720
crowbars, like a bunch of weapons.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.410
They were looting the
Nordstrom right here.

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:49.820
- [Narrator] Nearly three
fourths of US retailers

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:53.110
said they saw a spike in ORC in 2020,

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:55.970
according to a national
retail security survey.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.530
And many said the pandemic
has played a role.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:01.070
- As COVID influenced
the way America shops,

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:03.290
everybody was buying their goods online.

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:06.950
So it created this
incredible increase in demand

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:08.290
for online products.

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:10.810
Organized crime organizations stepped up

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.670
to fill that demand.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:14.440
- [Narrator] Ben Dugan
has been following trends

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.720
in retail crime for 30 years

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.150
and has worked with CVS
for the last four years

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:21.690
to investigate ORC incidents.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:24.220
He says members of ORC groups can target

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:27.760
as many as 15 to 20 stores in a single day

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:30.890
and often resell the stolen
goods as a third party seller

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.000
on various online marketplaces.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.350
- Well, the biggest challenge

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:37.080
when dealing with illicit
sellers on online marketplaces

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:38.810
first and foremost is who they are.

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:41.810
They do not have to provide
their real names or addresses

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:43.927
or banking information or information

00:01:43.927 --> 00:01:47.810
that any legitimate
business would provide.

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:50.460
- [Narrator] As CVS
Health's top investigator,

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:54.210
Dugan said he solved 27
cases of e-commerce crime

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:58.000
in 2020 alone, amounting
to nearly $50 million

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.150
worth of goods.

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:02.180
Earlier this year, a
bipartisan group of senators

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:04.940
introduced the Informed Consumers Act,

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:07.050
which would require e-commerce platforms

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:10.420
to verify high volume
third-party seller information,

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:14.260
ultimately making it more
difficult to sell stolen goods.

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.970
From locking up products and ramping up

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:19.070
physical security measures,
to installing GPS tracking

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:21.640
on products, stores are finding new ways

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:24.130
to combat potential ORC incidents,

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:26.823
specifically smash and grab robberies.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.950
- Retailers are doing a lot,

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:31.530
especially this holiday season.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.240
As always, the number one concern

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:35.260
for the retail community and industry

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:37.660
is to keep our employees
and our customers safe.

